Subject: [PATCH] usb: usbfs: correct kernel->user page attribute mismatch (4.9 backport)

Backport to 4.9 of three mainline commits which together give the
current mainline mapping logic of usbdev_mmap():

  2bef9aed6f0e usb: usbfs: correct kernel->user page attribute mismatch
               (Jeremy Linton <jeremy.linton@arm.com>)
  a0e710a7def4 USB: usbfs: fix mmap dma mismatch
               (Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>)
  d0b861653f8c usb: usbfs: Use consistent mmap functions
               (Ruihan Li <lrh2000@pku.edu.cn>)

From 2bef9aed6f0e:

  On some architectures (e.g. arm64) requests for IO coherent memory may
  use non-cachable attributes if the relevant device isn't cache
  coherent. If these pages are then remapped into userspace as
  cacheable, they may not be coherent with the non-cacheable mappings.
  [...] dma_mmap_coherent() can be used instead of remap_pfn_range().
  The page cache/etc attributes will then be correctly set in userspace
  to match the kernel mapping.

Adapted to 4.9, nothing else changed:
 - hcd->self.sysdev (4.11+) becomes hcd->self.controller, the device
   4.9's hcd_buffer_alloc() allocates on;
 - DMA_MAPPING_ERROR (4.20+) becomes its value, ~(dma_addr_t)0, which is
   what 4.9's hcd_buffer_alloc() stores when it falls back to kmalloc().

Seen on SigmaStar SSC338Q (Cortex-A7, 4.9.84): libusb zero-copy RX
buffers (libusb_dev_mem_alloc) read stale 64-byte cache lines from an
earlier transfer, about 1.5 per 1000 frames.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/core/devio.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/devio.c
@@ -224,10 +224,11 @@
 {
 	struct usb_memory *usbm = NULL;
 	struct usb_dev_state *ps = file->private_data;
+	struct usb_hcd *hcd = bus_to_hcd(ps->dev->bus);
 	size_t size = vma->vm_end - vma->vm_start;
 	void *mem;
 	unsigned long flags;
-	dma_addr_t dma_handle;
+	dma_addr_t dma_handle = ~(dma_addr_t) 0;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = usbfs_increase_memory_usage(size + sizeof(struct usb_memory));
@@ -257,11 +258,26 @@
 	usbm->vma_use_count = 1;
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&usbm->memlist);
 
-	if (remap_pfn_range(vma, vma->vm_start,
-			virt_to_phys(usbm->mem) >> PAGE_SHIFT,
-			size, vma->vm_page_prot) < 0) {
-		dec_usb_memory_use_count(usbm, &usbm->vma_use_count);
-		return -EAGAIN;
+	/*
+	 * In DMA-unavailable cases, hcd_buffer_alloc allocates normal
+	 * pages and assigns ~(dma_addr_t)0 to dma_handle. Check whether we
+	 * are in such cases, and then use remap_pfn_range (or
+	 * dma_mmap_coherent) to map normal (or DMA) pages into the user
+	 * space, respectively.
+	 */
+	if (dma_handle == ~(dma_addr_t) 0) {
+		if (remap_pfn_range(vma, vma->vm_start,
+				    virt_to_phys(usbm->mem) >> PAGE_SHIFT,
+				    size, vma->vm_page_prot) < 0) {
+			dec_usb_memory_use_count(usbm, &usbm->vma_use_count);
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		}
+	} else {
+		if (dma_mmap_coherent(hcd->self.controller, vma, mem,
+				      dma_handle, size)) {
+			dec_usb_memory_use_count(usbm, &usbm->vma_use_count);
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		}
 	}
 
 	vma->vm_flags |= VM_IO;
